!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/validate/valid/a-paged-get-operation-omits-its-pinned-method-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/validate-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §4.2, [TSON-SCHEMA] §5.2, [TSON-SCHEMA] §5.8, [TSON-SCHEMA] §7.4"
  description: """
    `paged_get` is an API description's own endpoint shape, a composition of the imported record type `operation`
    pinning `method` to `GET` under a marked name, so an operation read against it in a data document may omit
    the field. Its response's `body` is a `meta.type_ref` slot, judged by membership over the document's closure:
    `order_page`, an alias the description closes from its own parametric record, is a type there. The http
    project relies on a gateway reading operations against a description's endpoint shapes as ordinary data.
    """
  valid: _
}
